<title>SWITZERLAND: SAirGroup details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>SAirGroup details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender 1996 vs 1995:</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net loss		 497		 vs 161</p>
<p> Operating profit	     344		 vs 247</p>
<p> Net loss per share, Sfr    219		 vs 71</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit	 41		  vs 24</p>
<p> Extraordinary expenditure  739		 vs 366</p>
<p> Net extraordinary result   698 loss	  vs 342 loss</p>
<p> Pre-tax, pre-fin result    354 loss	  vs 96 loss</p>
<p> Net financial result	 85 loss	   vs 25 loss</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p> Result of shareholdings    35 loss	   vs 12</p>
<p> Finance results		50 loss	   vs 37</p>
<p> Taxes			    41		  vs 35</p>
<p> Operating cash flow	  873		 vs n.a.</p>
<p> Operating revenue	    8,212	     vs 7,028</p>
<p> incl. book gains	     87		  vs 52</p>
<p> Operating expenditure	7,895	     vs 6,781</p>
<p> Material expenditure	 3,593	     vs 2,718</p>
<p> incl. fuel costs	     3,593	     vs 2,718</p>
<p> Personnel expenditure	2,618	     vs 2,561</p>
<p> Other operating expense    1,056	     vs 909</p>
<p> Depreciation		   628		 vs 593</p>
<p> Profit from investments    27		  vs zero</p>
<p> Net loss incl. minorites   480		 vs 155</p>
<p> Minorities		     17 loss	   vs 6 loss</p>
<p> Workforce			36,050	    vs 32,703</p>
<p> Total assets		   11,817	    vs 11,024</p>
<p> Total shareholders' equity 2,109	     vs 2,510</p>
<p> of which: share capital    808		 vs 808</p>
<p> Reserves			 1,336	     vs 1,401</p>
<p> Liabilities		    9,509	     vs 8,335</p>
<p> of which:current liabil.   1,621	     vs 1,834</p>
<p> Non-current libilities     5,195	     vs 4,400</p>
<p> Provisions		     1,360	     vs 995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Swissair Schweizerische Luftverkehr AG.</p>
<p>Swissair will propose to shareholders on May 22 that it adopts a holding company structure and the group's name is changed to SAirGroup. Since December the company has called itself SAirGroup.</p>
<p>Swissair adopted International Accounting Standards (IAS) for the 1996 results. The 1995 group net profit was restated from an originally reported 147 million.</p>
<p>Book gains mainly come from the sale of four MD-81, 10 Fokker-100 and five Saab 340A aircraft.</p>
<p>-- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
